				\begin{document}$$ \sqrt{\mathrm{p}} $$\end{document}p [13, 14]. Thus, when p > 80 and likely still contained many noisy variables, we used an mtry of 0.1*p, and after features were recursively removed from the model and p ≤ 80, we used the default mtry. These parameters produced reasonably low MSEOOBs when compared to others. Permutation variable importance mode was used.
